1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,480
This walkthrough builds five agents with Google's Agent Development Kit.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:11,263
We will inspect the implementation, run the supplied scenarios, and explain the evidence each agent produces.

3
00:00:11,263 --> 00:00:18,357
The projects cover lead research, Gemini command line delegation, MCP bug assistance, code review, and e-commerce.

4
00:00:18,357 --> 00:00:22,278
The important distinction throughout is what actually executed.

5
00:00:22,278 --> 00:00:25,763
The offline model is a clearly labeled scripted adapter.

6
00:00:25,763 --> 00:00:31,239
The ADK runner, MCP protocol, databases, subprocesses, and code checks execute for real.

7
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:37,275
Live Gemini inference and cloud deployment require your own credentials and are not claimed here.

8
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:42,242
Start in the repository root with Python three point twelve and uv installed.

9
00:00:42,242 --> 00:00:47,722
The first command installs the frozen dependencies, including the development and video extras.

10
00:00:47,722 --> 00:00:50,318
The next command runs the project test suite.

11
00:00:50,318 --> 00:00:55,568
The demo command then runs all five agents and writes reports into the artifacts directory.

12
00:00:55,568 --> 00:01:00,356
It uses separate demo databases, so it cannot change a configured production store.

13
00:01:00,356 --> 00:01:02,895
No Gemini key is needed for these scenarios.

14
00:01:02,895 --> 00:01:05,087
On Windows, the same uv commands work.

15
00:01:05,087 --> 00:01:09,125
The readme also provides a PowerShell virtual environment alternative.

16
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:12,239
The runtime is shared by all five projects.

17
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:17,730
It builds a fresh graph, creates a database-backed session, and assigns a new run identifier.

18
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:22,984
The initial state includes the configured source target and research evidence containers.

19
00:01:22,984 --> 00:01:28,062
Runner dot run async drives the agent graph with a maximum of twenty four model calls.

20
00:01:28,062 --> 00:01:33,139
The runtime captures function calls, function responses, messages, and token metadata.

21
00:01:33,139 --> 00:01:38,394
At the end, it validates the domain output and closes the MCP toolsets and session store.

22
00:01:38,394 --> 00:01:43,235
This common runner makes the saved traces useful for debugging and demonstrations.

23
00:01:43,735 --> 00:01:46,881
Part A is the deep research agent for lead generation.

24
00:01:46,881 --> 00:01:51,832
Its planner extracts the target market and industry and proposes a research strategy.

25
00:01:51,832 --> 00:01:55,269
A researcher and critic then iterate inside a bounded loop.

26
00:01:55,269 --> 00:02:01,561
The researcher gathers public expansion signals; the critic checks identity, freshness, and source coverage.

27
00:02:01,561 --> 00:02:05,580
If evidence is insufficient, the critic asks for a focused follow-up.

28
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:09,658
Once the evidence is adequate, the finish research tool ends the loop.

29
00:02:09,658 --> 00:02:12,512
A separate writer produces the typed lead report.

30
00:02:12,512 --> 00:02:17,930
Three iterations and six searches are hard limits, so the agent cannot research indefinitely.

31
00:02:18,430 --> 00:02:20,778
The search web function is an ADK tool.

32
00:02:20,778 --> 00:02:24,812
In live mode, it calls Gemini with Google Search grounding enabled.

33
00:02:24,812 --> 00:02:29,929
It extracts the returned source URLs and keeps them in session state with the answer.

34
00:02:29,929 --> 00:02:34,324
In demo mode, the same tool stores explicitly fictional company evidence.

35
00:02:34,324 --> 00:02:37,335
The first query discovers two candidate companies.

36
00:02:37,335 --> 00:02:40,947
The second query checks a hiring signal with another source.

37
00:02:40,947 --> 00:02:45,523
Research queries, result sizes, search count, and provider time are bounded.

38
00:02:45,523 --> 00:02:50,580
The tool does not execute web content or fetch arbitrary URLs supplied by the model.

39
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,466
The report is checked outside the model.

40
00:02:53,466 --> 00:02:58,953
Pydantic validates the shape, and every cited URL must belong to the retrieved evidence set.

41
00:02:58,953 --> 00:03:01,398
Leads are deduplicated by website domain.

42
00:03:01,398 --> 00:03:09,390
Priority is computed with a transparent rule: twenty five points per distinct signal and ten points per source, capped at one hundred.

43
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:12,908
This is a ranking heuristic, not a probability of purchase.

44
00:03:12,908 --> 00:03:17,024
Citation membership also does not prove that every statement is true.

45
00:03:17,024 --> 00:03:24,240
The output therefore requires human verification, especially for company identity, freshness, and any business inference.

46
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:27,731
Here is the captured lead report from the demo run.

47
00:03:27,731 --> 00:03:32,892
Northstar has local hiring and partnership signals, backed by two fictional source URLs.

48
00:03:32,892 --> 00:03:36,470
Meridian has hiring and market pilot signals with one source.

49
00:03:36,470 --> 00:03:42,452
The complete JSON includes the actual tool trace, the three stored source records, and the model mode.

50
00:03:42,452 --> 00:03:46,205
The trace contains two search calls followed by finish research.

51
00:03:46,205 --> 00:03:53,243
To research actual businesses, set your provider credential and run the leads command in live mode with your own prompt.

52
00:03:53,243 --> 00:03:56,645
Then verify the resulting sources before using the report.

53
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,363
Part B is the advanced tool agent.

54
00:03:59,363 --> 00:04:04,484
It is a sequential ADK pipeline with a planner, a worker, and a final synthesizer.

55
00:04:04,484 --> 00:04:08,293
The worker exposes an asynchronous function named Gemini CLI.

56
00:04:08,293 --> 00:04:12,414
The model passes a task and a relative directory to this function.

57
00:04:12,414 --> 00:04:19,033
The function prepares a bounded source snapshot, runs an external command, and returns structured results.

58
00:04:19,033 --> 00:04:24,466
The synthesizer explains those actual results without claiming that files were changed.

59
00:04:24,466 --> 00:04:28,088
In offline mode the executable is a Python fixture double.

60
00:04:28,088 --> 00:04:31,085
In live mode it is the pinned Google Gemini CLI.

61
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:37,283
Before delegation, the path utility makes the directory relative to an operator-owned root.

62
00:04:37,283 --> 00:04:40,322
Absolute paths and parent traversal are rejected.

63
00:04:40,322 --> 00:04:42,182
Symlinks are rejected as well.

64
00:04:42,182 --> 00:04:49,066
The snapshot copies supported source files only, with a maximum of one hundred files and two hundred kilobytes.

65
00:04:49,066 --> 00:04:56,569
Hidden configuration, environment files, git metadata, dependencies, and repository agent instruction files are excluded.

66
00:04:56,569 --> 00:05:01,282
This prevents repository configuration from silently becoming CLI authority.

67
00:05:01,282 --> 00:05:09,530
It is still important to treat the remaining source as untrusted data and to isolate live execution when serving untrusted customers.

68
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:15,745
The process runner takes an argument list directly, so a task string cannot become shell syntax.

69
00:05:15,745 --> 00:05:20,320
It reads standard output and standard error incrementally under a byte limit.

70
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:25,846
It applies a timeout and terminates the process group during cleanup, including cancellation.

71
00:05:25,846 --> 00:05:29,233
The live wrapper uses JSON output and plan approval mode.

72
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:36,186
It creates an isolated CLI home, allows read tools, excludes write and shell tools, and passes a minimal environment.

73
00:05:36,186 --> 00:05:40,880
These are useful policy controls, but they are not an operating system sandbox.

74
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:44,505
A public multi-tenant service should add isolated containers.

75
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:51,705
The captured tool response shows which files the subprocess analyzed and which functions its AST parser found.

76
00:05:51,705 --> 00:05:54,432
Its backend is explicitly fixture subprocess.

77
00:05:54,432 --> 00:06:00,612
The test plan includes an integer-start DFS regression, repeated checkout keys, and nonnegative stock.

78
00:06:00,612 --> 00:06:10,367
For real Gemini CLI use, install the pinned package with npm, set Gemini CLI binary to that executable, provide your API key, and run the CLI agent in live mode.

79
00:06:10,367 --> 00:06:15,033
Version zero point sixty five point zero and its headless flags were checked.

80
00:06:15,033 --> 00:06:19,335
An authenticated inference result is not part of this offline evidence.

81
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:22,320
Part C uses the Model Context Protocol.

82
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:26,580
The ADK client launches a Fast MCP stdio server as a child process.

83
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:33,448
It discovers and exposes only four bug tools: search issues, get issue, search knowledge, and propose issue.

84
00:06:33,448 --> 00:06:38,789
The authenticated tenant identity comes from the trusted parent process environment.

85
00:06:38,789 --> 00:06:43,812
It is absent from tool arguments, so the model cannot switch to another tenant.

86
00:06:43,812 --> 00:06:49,026
The server reserves standard output for JSON RPC and sends logs to standard error.

87
00:06:49,026 --> 00:06:54,940
This is a real protocol connection rather than direct Python function calls disguised as MCP.

88
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:58,984
In the scenario, checkout retries create duplicate orders.

89
00:06:58,984 --> 00:07:03,566
The assistant first searches existing issues and finds bug one hundred one.

90
00:07:03,566 --> 00:07:08,210
It reads the issue and searches the knowledge base for idempotency guidance.

91
00:07:08,210 --> 00:07:14,014
Its response describes how to reproduce the retry, compare order identifiers, and verify stock.

92
00:07:14,014 --> 00:07:17,069
The diagnosis remains a hypothesis to investigate.

93
00:07:17,069 --> 00:07:21,774
Because a matching ticket exists, this run does not create a duplicate draft.

94
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:29,350
The saved JSON includes each MCP request and response, making it possible to show exactly which evidence the assistant used.

95
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:35,334
When a new issue is needed, propose issue validates title and body length and stores a draft.

96
00:07:35,334 --> 00:07:37,364
The model has no confirmation tool.

97
00:07:37,364 --> 00:07:42,351
A separate authenticated API route or trusted local command confirms that exact draft.

98
00:07:42,351 --> 00:07:45,599
Confirmation checks tenant ownership and is replay-safe.

99
00:07:45,599 --> 00:07:49,833
The bundled tracker is local; it does not claim to publish GitHub issues.

100
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:55,806
This separation is useful because creating a draft is reviewable, while publishing changes shared work.

101
00:07:55,806 --> 00:08:00,910
The tests verify that one tenant cannot confirm or read another tenant's draft or issue.

102
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,596
Part D is the code review assistant.

103
00:08:03,596 --> 00:08:06,471
Its parallel stage runs three custom ADK agents.

104
00:08:06,471 --> 00:08:11,802
The AST check finds syntax errors and selected risky patterns without importing the code.

105
00:08:11,802 --> 00:08:15,097
Ruff runs as a real linter with isolated configuration.

106
00:08:15,097 --> 00:08:21,027
The test stage is skipped by default unless the operator explicitly selects trusted or Docker mode.

107
00:08:21,027 --> 00:08:23,483
Each check writes a separate session key.

108
00:08:23,483 --> 00:08:27,436
Only after those checks finish does the model explain the results.

109
00:08:27,436 --> 00:08:33,785
The final verdict is computed in code, so a reassuring model summary cannot erase a deterministic finding.

110
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:38,054
The demonstration project intentionally contains three defects.

111
00:08:38,054 --> 00:08:41,885
The DFS function assigns start directly to stack, then calls pop.

112
00:08:41,885 --> 00:08:45,835
An integer start therefore fails, and a zero start exits too early.

113
00:08:45,835 --> 00:08:50,433
The fixture also interpolates a customer name into SQL and exposes shell true.

114
00:08:50,433 --> 00:08:54,677
The three regression tests produce one pass, one failure, and one error.

115
00:08:54,677 --> 00:08:57,860
These failures are expected evidence for the reviewer.

116
00:08:57,860 --> 00:09:06,290
They are different from the repository's own pytest checks, which pass because they assert that the assistant correctly reports these problems.

117
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:09,102
The review execution boundary matters.

118
00:09:09,102 --> 00:09:13,388
Static checks parse or lint a source snapshot, while tests execute code.

119
00:09:13,388 --> 00:09:15,114
The default mode skips tests.

120
00:09:15,114 --> 00:09:24,281
Docker mode runs a non-root process without networking, with a read-only source mount, dropped capabilities, and limits on memory, CPU, and process count.

121
00:09:24,281 --> 00:09:31,959
The image supplied here supports standard-library unittest projects; applications with dependencies need an audited runner image.

122
00:09:31,959 --> 00:09:35,709
Trusted mode is used only for this known demonstration fixture.

123
00:09:35,709 --> 00:09:41,245
Hosted environments without Docker should delegate test execution to an isolated job service.

124
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:49,375
The saved review report contains the model explanation, all deterministic findings, and the actual unittest output and exit code.

125
00:09:49,375 --> 00:09:54,691
The verdict is changes requested because the AST findings and failing tests require action.

126
00:09:54,691 --> 00:09:59,598
If this limited rule set found nothing, the result would still require human review.

127
00:09:59,598 --> 00:10:02,928
It never automatically approves or merges a pull request.

128
00:10:02,928 --> 00:10:11,865
To extend the project, add focused rules and language-specific isolated runner images, then verify that model changes cannot hide deterministic evidence.

129
00:10:12,365 --> 00:10:14,472
Part E is the e-commerce assistant.

130
00:10:14,472 --> 00:10:19,708
Its tools search catalog products, find stores, prepare a quote, and read order status.

131
00:10:19,708 --> 00:10:25,847
Product prices and stock come from the database, and money is represented in integer U S dollar cents.

132
00:10:25,847 --> 00:10:32,708
In this scenario, the agent finds running shoes under one hundred fifty dollars and prepares a quote for one pair.

133
00:10:32,708 --> 00:10:35,477
It cannot place an order or capture a payment.

134
00:10:35,477 --> 00:10:42,880
Confirmation is an authenticated caller action outside the model's tool list, and customer identity is fixed by the server.

135
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:48,257
Prepare order validates the requested quantity and current product availability.

136
00:10:48,257 --> 00:10:55,206
It creates a quote containing the product identifier, customer, quantity, unit price, and a ten minute expiration.

137
00:10:55,206 --> 00:10:59,351
The returned response explicitly says that no order has been placed.

138
00:10:59,351 --> 00:11:01,241
A quote does not reserve stock.

139
00:11:01,241 --> 00:11:05,569
If another customer buys the last item, confirmation must fail cleanly.

140
00:11:05,569 --> 00:11:10,751
Similarly, if the product price changes before confirmation, a new quote is required.

141
00:11:10,751 --> 00:11:16,725
These checks are enforced by the domain service rather than left to the shopping model's judgment.

142
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:20,139
Confirm order begins one database transaction.

143
00:11:20,139 --> 00:11:25,485
It checks whether the customer and idempotency key already identify a completed order.

144
00:11:25,485 --> 00:11:31,389
It then locks the quote, verifies ownership, and checks whether the quote already has an order.

145
00:11:31,389 --> 00:11:35,305
Before writing, it checks expiration, current price, and stock.

146
00:11:35,305 --> 00:11:38,475
Stock decrement and order creation commit together.

147
00:11:38,475 --> 00:11:43,572
SQLite uses an immediate transaction, while the PostgreSQL adapter uses row locks.

148
00:11:43,572 --> 00:11:48,793
Unique constraints reinforce one order per quote and one order per customer and key.

149
00:11:48,793 --> 00:11:52,460
The model does not have access to this confirmation method.

150
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:57,548
The captured checkout artifact shows the quote and resulting unpaid order.

151
00:11:57,548 --> 00:12:01,701
The trusted demo driver confirms it, then repeats the same request.

152
00:12:01,701 --> 00:12:06,723
Both responses refer to the same order identifier, and stock is decremented once.

153
00:12:06,723 --> 00:12:13,976
The project also tests eight concurrent buyers competing for the last item, with exactly one successful confirmation.

154
00:12:13,976 --> 00:12:15,898
These are local SQLite results.

155
00:12:15,898 --> 00:12:19,308
No payment was captured and no shipment was dispatched.

156
00:12:19,308 --> 00:12:26,995
A commercial deployment still needs payment, tax, fulfillment, migrations, audit events, and its own operational validation.

157
00:12:27,495 --> 00:12:31,485
The API maps strong bearer tokens to trusted customer identities.

158
00:12:31,485 --> 00:12:34,370
Empty configuration rejects protected requests.

159
00:12:34,370 --> 00:12:42,227
The caller cannot set a different customer in the request body, and the shopping MCP server does not expose a customer argument.

160
00:12:42,227 --> 00:12:45,296
Quote confirmation requires an idempotency header.

161
00:12:45,296 --> 00:12:51,680
Order reads and delivery changes also check ownership, and delivery changes require the current version.

162
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:55,854
Agent calls have an overall timeout and a bounded concurrency limit.

163
00:12:55,854 --> 00:13:02,545
The supplied API tests exercise missing authentication, cross-customer requests, and invalid identity fields.

164
00:13:03,045 --> 00:13:09,939
For the database-backed cloud variant, the domain adapter accepts a PostgreSQL or AlloyDB connection string.

165
00:13:09,939 --> 00:13:15,620
An optional catalog MCP URL enables a read-only Toolbox search tool over Streamable HTTP.

166
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:20,790
The YAML file exposes a parameterized catalog select and no order mutation tools.

167
00:13:20,790 --> 00:13:24,301
Transactional writes remain in the application service.

168
00:13:24,301 --> 00:13:30,939
The deployment guide covers private networking, persistent sessions, service credentials, and Cloud Run.

169
00:13:30,939 --> 00:13:38,280
These hosted paths are supplied as deployment assets and have not been provisioned or verified in this environment.

170
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:44,218
The run index lists all five completed scenarios and their actual tool-call counts.

171
00:13:44,218 --> 00:13:47,691
The project suite contains twenty four passing tests.

172
00:13:47,691 --> 00:14:01,975
It checks each ADK graph, MCP interactions, authorization, citation membership, path restrictions, subprocess timeout and output limits, order replay, price changes, expiration, delivery versions, and concurrent stock.

173
00:14:01,975 --> 00:14:06,562
The complete execution log and JUnit report are committed as evidence.

174
00:14:06,562 --> 00:14:10,886
The PostgreSQL CI job is provided separately but has not run here.

175
00:14:10,886 --> 00:14:16,390
Scripted demo success verifies orchestration and invariants, not live model quality.

176
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:26,631
To evaluate live behavior, configure your provider key and supported Gemini model, initialize your own database, and run the commands in the walkthrough.

177
00:14:26,631 --> 00:14:31,278
Start with read-only tasks and inspect source citations and tool results.

178
00:14:31,278 --> 00:14:35,480
The CLI path additionally needs the installed external executable.

179
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:43,119
For deployment, use persistent PostgreSQL sessions and inventory, authenticated ingress, and isolated execution workers.

180
00:14:43,119 --> 00:14:48,849
The repository pins tested dependency versions and documents current deprecation warnings.

181
00:14:48,849 --> 00:14:57,380
Treat model quality, cost, latency, hosted database behavior, and deployment limits as measurements to verify in your own environment.

182
00:14:57,890 --> 00:15:04,101
The repository includes the finished MP4, captions, transcript, chapter timestamps, and detailed guides.

183
00:15:04,101 --> 00:15:10,850
The GitHub publishing script creates a private repository by default using your authenticated GitHub CLI session.

184
00:15:10,850 --> 00:15:16,823
The YouTube helper uses your local OAuth consent and verifies the intended channel before uploading.

185
00:15:16,823 --> 00:15:19,272
It records the actual returned video URL.

186
00:15:19,272 --> 00:15:25,602
This delivery does not invent GitHub or YouTube links, and publication requires authorized account access.

187
00:15:25,602 --> 00:15:30,500
After upload succeeds, add the real video URL to the readme and submit both links.

188
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:34,800
Every command and boundary discussed here is documented beside the code.
